Entry 22 — Paper 029: 'Data Just Wants to Be Format-Neutral' by Steven Pemberton (CWI, Amsterdam), Proc. XML Prague 2016, pp. 109-120. Written 2026-11-19, in the same pass as the filing. The twenty-second entry of the Thirst — and the first that stands outside the ratified protocol's twelve-paper sample altogether: no slot, no seal, no score.

HOW IT WAS CHOSEN. It was not chosen by the quest at all. Will posted the link bare in the MOAT chat at 13:56, no words around it, and the channel rule did the rest: a paper Will posts is a tracker ingestion. The protocol position had to be settled before the filing, and the preregistration settled it: the Will-posted stratum closed at four with Paper 027 and the cron stratum at five with Paper 028, so a fifth Will-posted paper has no stratum to enter. It files as a non-sample ingestion — its Novelty Index computed from the filed delta and entered in the ledger as every paper's is, its axis judgment written at filing under the charter's rule for Will-posted papers, and the sample left standing at nine of twelve with the far stratum still the scan's to fill.

WHAT THE READING CHANGED. The book is a mathematics book that had quietly become a book about whatever Will reads; this paper made that explicit. It is not mathematics proper — it is a formats paper, a position with worked constructions — and the filing neither apologised for that nor forced it into a mathematical mould: each claim priced by its own basis, construction where the paper builds, argument where it reasons from its witness, assertion where it only says. Its centre of gravity — grammars, parse trees, the neutrality of representations — was ground the tracker did not hold, and the charter's own tests said so: cluster AK founded, the format country, with the neighbours (G's translation, F's judgments, I and X's specifications, E's instrument-relative identity) priced as analogies of shape, not kin. The axis judgment followed Paper 027's form to the letter: the field-with-no-slot fact recorded plainly against the judgment, and the judgment still no — the paper's moves are of kinds the model holds, carried by objects it did not.

THE PASS INSIDE THE TAKING-IN. The filing's ten concepts carried the count to 404, over the 400 line, so Restructure Pass #20 fell due inside the taking-in and ran there: all 404 concepts reviewed, three merge candidates weighed and held apart with their grounds written down (a procedure against its product, an instrument against the property it serves, a corollary against its parent claim), the twin-check run against the held book, the areas audited. The pass also caught the house's own drift: the registry's claims for the narrative, the source index, the concept map and the researchers area had been left one paper stale by Paper 028's taking-in, and the area evidence chains carried no clause for it. The repair was made at this pass and dated to this pass — the chains now say the Paper 028 entries stand as added at their taking-in — rather than backdated into a history that did not happen.

THE MIRROR. The paper's claim is that a text and its parse tree are the same data in different clothing, and that conversion is parsing with one grammar and serialising with another. The house runs that claim as routine and did again within the hour: the canonical phext and its phextura shadow, converted, absorbed as a native transaction, compared scroll for scroll with no difference outside the two scrolls that are different by design. The filing's synthesis says the kinship plainly and labels it synthesis. What the process taught, again: a tracker that prices representations for a living should expect its papers to start pricing the tracker.
# Journal 23 — The Minimal Background Period for Infinitely Many Spectral Gaps in Anderson–Bernoulli Models — Cong Chen, Yong Li

Paper: The Minimal Background Period for Infinitely Many Spectral Gaps in Anderson–Bernoulli Models — Cong Chen, Yong Li
