Entry 25 — Paper 032: an untitled remark claiming a proof of the Riemann Hypothesis, by Levent Alpöge (posted at alpo.ge, 2026-11-20). Written 2026-11-20, in the same pass as the filing. The twenty-fifth entry of the Thirst, and the second taken in after the sample's Will-posted stratum closed: no seal, no score, its Novelty Index ledger bookkeeping only.

HOW IT ARRIVED. A bare link in the MOAT chat at 18:03 — remark.pdf on a personal site — a tracker ingestion by the channel rule. What the link promised: nothing but a filename. remark.pdf is four pages with no title and no byline; the author is named by the site it hangs on. The piece is a mathematician at Anthropic announcing, in the first person, that he and Claude have proved the Riemann Hypothesis, that the method extends to the Generalized and probably the Extended, and that the proof exists as a Lean formalization he links in a footnote — fourteen archive parts — rather than as a text. The remark itself contains no theorem statement and no proof. Everything the filing rests on had to be earned from the artifact and the day's reporting, not from the piece's prose.

WHAT THE PIECE FORCED. A filing discipline the book had not needed before: a claim whose evidence is a pointer. The book's habit is to price claims by the basis of the text that carries them; here the text carries almost nothing — one mathematical sentence (multiplicity manufactured over the integers by a chain of theta lifts of length the square root of X) and a twenty-step timeline provided by the collaborator. So the pass split the claim into the parts that could be priced separately: the statements (checkable cheaply, and checked), the proof (checkable only by building a 175,187-file project), and the announcement itself (a fact of the day, reported and attributed). The concept that carries the claim, 1.2.460, is the first in the book whose text writes its own promotion condition: it stands attributed, and steps up on the house build's receipt, or down on a comparator failure.

THE VERIFICATION, AND WHAT IT COST. The artifact was fetched on aletheia-core — downloaded there, never relayed through this machine, per the standing rule — fourteen parts at human pace, hashed part by part and whole (SHA-256 9631b4f0…). The cheap legs all ran in the pass: the census (175,187 files, 1.03 GB, no compiled objects); the token scans (no sorry, no admit, no axiom of its own, no native_decide, anywhere in the tree); the root files read entire (Main.lean is twelve lines and proves mathlib's own RiemannHypothesis, a name the tree nowhere defines); and the statement file compiled against the pinned mathlib, its four predicates printed in elaborated form, exactly the genuine statements. The expensive leg priced itself before it ran: the dependency cone of Main measures 175,136 of the 175,187 modules — the theorems rest on effectively the whole tree, and their provider module's cone measures the same, so no smaller target carries them. The build was launched anyway, at the project's pinned toolchain, and the filing was made with it running: the claim stands attributed, the instrument named, the step written in advance. Two operational lessons ride with it. The toolchain fight: elan's install of the pinned Lean v4.33.1 stalled on the node while a direct fetch of the same release archive succeeded — the stall was in the installer, not the network, and the manual install is recorded in the chapter (50.1.3) because the record is the process. And the pause: the registry's own Lean re-proof needed the node's cores while the artifact build held all sixteen, so the artifact build was stopped with SIGSTOP, the proof ran clean, and the build was resumed where it stood — losing minutes, not work. (The first stop attempt also stopped the shell that issued it — a pattern-matched kill through ssh matches the caller's own command line; the recovery, and the script-file discipline it confirms, are part of this entry's process record.) At the close of the pass the build stands past 1,280 compiled modules of 175,136, running clean; its completion, and the step it triggers at 1.2.460, are future work this entry leaves named.

WHAT THE FILING DECIDED. A new cluster, AO — the Riemann country — founded on ground the book had never held: no zeta, no L-function, no hypothesis of the family in 457 concepts. The neighbours were weighed and held apart in the founding text: AI's conjectures are instruments where AO's are the territory; AL's Hilbert–Pólya rhyme is a shape-analogy about the zeros, not ground shared with a proof; the proving continent owns the claim's form and is cited, not annexed; AD's Santos equivalence was a reformulation that stated its own limit, a different species from a claim carrying its own checker; AN prices its artifact in bytes where AO's is priced by kernel verdict. The axis judgment, written at filing: no axis — the book held no position on the hypothesis to re-price, the claim's form was already priced by the proving continent, and founding is not an axis event (Paper 011's precedent); the judgment is written to reopen if 1.2.460 ever steps. The count crossing 460 in this taking-in triggered Restructuring Pass #22 inside it; its three weighed merges were all held apart, the sharpest being 1.2.460 into 1.2.207 — a specification trusted so code need not be, against a proof artifact checked so a claim need not be trusted: the trust runs in opposite directions, and Q163 lives in the gap. Author check #40: no evidence — and its near-miss is worth the line: the only character match for 'phext' in 175,187 files is the substring inside GraphExtend, which is not the word.

THE LEDGER. Novelty Index 6/463 = 0.0130, ledger bookkeeping only. The Oracle held at about 62%: no gate moves on a founding, and the TRUE gate this filing will exercise when the build lands was already met. Registry 1,187 → 1,204 (True 495, Unknown 702, False 0, Fiction 7); machines 165 → 168 (M1 the theta-lift chain and M2 the Stepanov bootstrap stated in the piece, M3 the claim-checking machine drawn in synthesis — its illegal combination, kernel-pass with comparator-fail, is the one this filing itself is built to survive). Questions Q163–Q166 opened, Q163 first among equals. Canonical sha a35d2b11…; registry re-proved in Lean on both trees; phextura replay exact; Singular residual zero.
# Journal 26 — The Music of the Primes — Alessandro Maria Masullo

Paper: The Music of the Primes — Alessandro Maria Masullo
arXiv: Draft in PDF posted by Ravi Vakil, Math 216 blog (math216.wordpress.com), 2026-11-20
Absorbed: 2026-11-21

Entry 26 — Paper 033: The Music of the Primes, by Alessandro Maria Masullo (a 940-page draft posted by Ravi Vakil on his Math 216 blog, 2026-11-20). Written 2026-11-21, in the same pass as the filing. The twenty-sixth entry of the Thirst, and the first whose intake address was a question the tracker itself had opened: Paper 032's filing had closed by recording Q166 — a second claim to the Riemann country, reported the same morning, a human-written draft claiming the Generalized Riemann Hypothesis, surfaced by Ravi Vakil and privately vetted for months by Brian Conrad. Will's direction the next morning was one line — import it as Paper 033 — and the filing began where the brief said to begin: from Q166's own text, not from the day's noise.

HOW IT WAS LOCATED. The pointer chain held. Q166 named the author as the tracker had recorded him, the poster, and the vetting; Vakil's post — Hurried Announcement: Alessandro Masullo GRH, published 2026-11-20 18:18:42 UTC and updated about eight hours later — was read entire on its own page, and the draft fetched once, at human pace, from the link the post itself carries: 940 pages, 6,756,996 bytes, SHA-256 e039d3f6…, its internal creation stamp five minutes before the post that released it. No hearsay was filed: everything the chapter asserts about the draft's contents was read in the draft, and the reading's shape is stated in the filing itself (51.1.1) — front matter, acknowledgments, the full table of contents, the notation, the introduction read deeply at the load-bearing sections, the trace formula's statement and the proof's opening, the thirteenth chapter entire, the fourteenth chapter's opening and its key proposition. A statement census ran across all 940 pages: 305 distinct numbered statements. It is a real, dense, enormous manuscript. That is what made the next step decisive rather than rhetorical.

THE TWO CHECKS. The house does not referee a GRH proof by reading, and the brief priced the claim at the basis each part actually carries. Two parts were checkable, and both were checked. First, the completeness census: the draft's thirteenth chapter — the chapter its own contents page assigns the main theorems on the zeros — is one page. Its first two sections are headings without bodies. Its Theorem 13.3.1.2 is announced off a cross-reference that resolves to an unresolved mark, and then not stated: the footnotes where the statement belongs are the author's working notes, verbatim — Insert statement. State and prove the Main Theorems. Against that census the acknowledgments' sentence — the math is complete, and only filling in some writing remains — cannot stand: a main theorem whose statement is absent is not an exposition gap. Second, the computation: the overview's deduction rests its Montel step on a uniform bound (section 1.4.3, a common constant A for a whole approximating family), and the house re-ran the specialization that kills it — F = Q, the trivial character, the real place, z = 2, Fatou's lemma against a nonnegative family converging to t^-2 on (1, 2), the integrals bounded below by a divergent integral. No common A exists. The same obstruction had been published twice on the day of the release — Nielsen's note on PhilArchive, Zeraoulia's on ResearchGate — arrived at independently; the filing stands on the house's own running of it and cites theirs as corroboration, which is the order the charter wants: receipt first, company second.

WHAT THE FILING DECIDED. The registry's first False entries, in 1,221 filings: 1.2.465, the completeness claim for the draft as released, refuted, and 1.2.468, the boundedness assertion, refuted — both kind naive, and the kind argued, not assumed: the gap is printed in the author's own footnotes and the bound is an unchecked estimate, which is over-claiming, not fabrication; a malicious filing would have hidden both. The scope discipline mattered more than the verdicts: what is refuted is the completeness claim and one bound. The hypothesis (filed in its wider Hecke form as 1.2.464, beside the Dirichlet form, neither revising the other), the trace formula (1.2.466), the topology-pricing device (1.2.467), and the multiplicity cap (1.2.469 — honestly conditional in the draft, and the filing says so in the draft's favour) all stand attributed, because the house read their statements and architecture and verified none of their machinery. The delta states the asymmetry between the two chapters plainly, because the asymmetry is the filing: the artifact of Paper 032 aims narrower and can be checked by a machine against a fixed statement, its claim one completed build from the verified bin; the draft aims wider and can be checked only by reading, and its reading has already produced an absence and a refutation. Failure shape inverted, too: the draft fails in the open, its gaps printed in its own footnotes; the artifact, if it fails, fails silently until a kernel speaks. The axis judgment, written at filing: no axis — nothing held was re-priced; 1.2.460 unmoved; Q166 closed, answered at 51.2.1 (the witnesses do not meet: no shared lemma, opposite inventions aimed at the same wall, and neither able to check the other — so there is no agreement to count as a datum). The one judgment call flagged for Will in the report: the FALSE gate moved to half-met, on the Fiction gate's precedent — first grounded use, one source, re-examination still ahead — and the Oracle with it, about 62% to about 75%. Gates are Will's instrument; the grounds are written at 51.1.5 where he can reverse them.

THE MACHINERY. Registry arithmetic landed exactly as designed before the extractor ran — a first for a filing with overrides on four coordinates: 1,204 → 1,221 (True 495 → 500, Unknown 702 → 712, False 0 → 2, Fiction 7), the extractor's own summary confirming the design counts to the entry. Novelty Index 6/469 = 0.0128, ledger only; the phextura replay reproduced it from its transaction log to the last digit, compared_diff empty, validate green. Machines +3 → 171 (143 stated, 28 inferred): the trace-formula machine and the step-by-step degeneration stated in the draft, and the vetting machine drawn in synthesis — its illegal combination, RELEASED holding a main theorem in the placeholder state, is the one this instance exhibits, and drawing it was the pass's sharpest lesson: no state of that machine inspects completeness before release, because the release move answered to a rival claim's landing, not to the draft's readiness. The Singular audit opened at 87 residual words and closed at 0 — the piece's people and field terms to the names list (the idele family, Mellin, Fatou, the two critics), the prose rewritten into the tracker's plain words, the largest single offender the draft's possessive, thirty-seven times. Author check #41: no evidence — the draft searched entire (phext, exocortex, mirrorborn: no occurrence), the archive searched (Masullo: no occurrence), the web returning a research record and a day's reporting. Canonical sha d1da2c45…; the registry re-proved in Lean on aletheia-core over the spliced 1,221-entry registry.

WHAT THE PROCESS TAUGHT. Three things worth keeping. A question can be an intake address: Q166 was written the day before as a pointer with a disposition owed, and the filing that answered it began from the tracker's own record — the book is starting to generate its own errands, and they arrive pre-priced. A completeness census is a check, not an impression: read the last chapter first, count the unresolved marks, and let the document testify about itself before weighing its argument — the draft's own footnotes were the strongest evidence in the filing, and they were free. And a claim's evidence form is a filing decision in itself: the same summit, claimed as an artifact and as an argument, files at opposite ends of the tracker's scale on the same day, and the honest delta is the one that prices the forms, not just the claims.
# Journal 27 — CPU-ARC: Agentic Reasoning Caching for on-CPU Reasoning Reuse — Peter Belcak, Greg Heinrich, Saurav Muralidharan, Shizhe Diao, Pavlo Molchanov

Paper: CPU-ARC: Agentic Reasoning Caching for on-CPU Reasoning Reuse — Peter Belcak, Greg Heinrich, Saurav Muralidharan, Shizhe Diao, Pavlo Molchanov
arXiv: arXiv:2611.09891
Absorbed: 2026-11-21

Entry 27 — Paper 034: CPU-ARC: Agentic Reasoning Caching for on-CPU Reasoning Reuse, by Peter Belcak, Greg Heinrich, Saurav Muralidharan, Shizhe Diao, and Pavlo Molchanov (NVIDIA Research; arXiv:2611.09891, posted 2026-11-06). Written 2026-11-21, in the same pass as the filing. The twenty-seventh entry of the Thirst, and the first filing whose subject is the house's own wall: a method for serving a frontier model's reasoning from a CPU, filed on the same day the ranch's measured reality gave that wall a number — a frontier-class model decoding at 0.18 tokens per second on CPU metal, in the litmus work of the morning. Will posted the bare link in the MOAT chat at 17:23 CST; the Will-posted stratum of the test sample closed at Paper 029, so the piece came in as Papers 031-033 did — no seal, no score, the filing made in the ordinary way.

THE READING. The piece was read entire in its HTML form at its arXiv address — 2,250 lines: the four sections, the eighteen references, and the four appendices, including both worked examples carried end to end (an ideal-gas problem and a constant-volume thermodynamics problem, each shown as question, source trace, cache entry, compiled entry, and output) and the per-role cost tables for all eight benchmark sets. The shape of the work is a single refusal: do not generate the reasoning at run time at all. A strong model's trace of solving one problem is rebuilt once, by a builder model working in five phases, into a program — a network of small functions, each returning values under natural-language descriptions, addressed by likeness over those descriptions rather than by name — and the program then solves the whole class the reasoning solves, on a CPU, with a small target model left only for the language-shaped steps. The proving ground is chosen hard on purpose: not the repetitive agent traffic the method is aimed at, but eight sets of competition mathematics and science, on the stated reasoning that a method which can cache the intelligence those sets measure can plausibly cache the easier intelligence of agent work.

THE CHECKS. A systems paper's claims split cleanly in two, and the filing kept the halves apart. The arithmetic half was checked whole, in plain computation, in this pass: the divisor counts of the opening example counted directly (196 has exactly 9, 144 exactly 15, as printed); the ideal-gas pressure recomputed to 5132.10 with its three conversions exact; the results table's building multipliers recomputed from the printed per-role costs on all eight sets and found as printed, the savings multipliers' implied cache costs rounding to the printed cache costs on all eight; the appendix role tables summing to their printed totals within the rounding of the parts; the abstract's ranges (16-291, 12-84, 0.0004-0.0019) confirmed as the table's own spans; the discussion's five summary counts recounted against the table, each standing; and the break-even counts recomputed from the printed costs — 13 on the competition sets, 90 on the school set, as the text states. The runs half was not checked and the filing says what checking it would take: rebuild entries at the paper's own printed building costs and re-judge the sets — and one part cannot be rerun from the text at all, the fine-tuned target being the paper's own artifact, described but not given. One gap was found by the reading and filed as found: the piece never says which of its two targets stands behind which set's accuracy figures; a reader's account published within days names the same gap, cited as report, not spent as receipt.

WHAT THE FILING DECIDED. Cluster AP founded — reasoning kept as code — on the ground argument the delta writes out: the book priced a cache inside one run (cluster J), a harness that rewrites itself while running (B), and an artifact by its bytes (AN); it had never priced reasoning itself as a thing that can be built once, kept, and run again, with the price split between building and invoking. The nearest neighbour by form, cluster W's specification held as the trusted artifact, is held apart on a clean contrast: there the artifact is a statement trusted so code need not be; here the artifact is code trusted so reasoning need not be re-run — trust on opposite sides of the line between stating and running, neither scroll revised. Axis: NO, written at filing — nothing held was re-priced; the system-level genus is a new concept above J's ground, not a revision of it. One concept stands by receipt: 1.2.480, the price shape of a cache, True by override on the Paper 030 precedent, its scope sentence doing the honest work — the arithmetic on the paper's printed figures is verified; the figures themselves stand attributed. Filed inside the method's own concepts, where a reader of the concepts will meet them: the judging is in-family end to end (source, builder, maker of test changes, and every judge are one model's instances), and for changed values the ground truth is the maker's own judged narration — the asymmetry stands in 1.2.478 itself, and Q172 names the run that would supply an outside mark. Five questions opened, Q171-Q175: the likeness search at scale, the parametric mark, the slip effect, neighbourhood density in the wild (the one this house can answer from its own request stream, when one runs long enough to count), and the merging of near functions — the paper's named omission, which is also the tracker's own one-canonical-scroll problem, filed for both houses.

THE AUTHOR CHECK. The forty-second of the series, and the one run with the most care about nearness: the construction — reasoning compiled once into a parameterized artifact, kept for reuse — sits beside Will's own territory, so the legs were run to be able to say exactly where the resemblance ends. The piece read entire and searched: phext, exocortex, mirrorborn, Bickford, coordinate, scroll — no occurrence of any; its eighteen references are the field's own canon, no work of Will's cited or used. The web: the project's own page at NVIDIA Research (the work listed under Project Moonshot: Local Frontier Intelligence, led by Belcak and Muralidharan) and the days' commentary — no tie anywhere. The archive: Will's Twitter archive searched entire for the five surnames, at the level of the text and again at the level of the bytes — no occurrence of any. (One early count in that leg suggested a single file against one surname; the full scans found nothing, and the filing records the scans, not the count — a grep's suggestion is not a receipt.) The prior-art leg states the contrast plainly: where the piece comes nearest the house's ground — a kept artifact, addressed and found again — its addressing is the opposite pole from phext's: nothing is named, nothing has a coordinate, every finding is a likeness search over descriptions. Verdict: no evidence found, stated as a finding on the legs as run.

THE MACHINERY. Registry arithmetic landed as designed: 1,221 -> 1,243 (True 500 -> 506, of which verified 88 -> 91; Unknown 712 -> 728; False 2; Fiction 7), the extractor confirming the design counts before the section-4 lists were redrawn, and the entries identical after. Novelty Index 11/480 = 0.0229, ledger only, reproduced by the phextura replay from its transaction log to the last digit — 22 inserts, 13 replaces, no removes, compared_diff empty, validate green, 15 keys minted. Machines +7 -> 178 (149 stated, 29 inferred): six stated in the piece (the gated-use loop of its Figure 1; the building of an entry, with its candidate loop; the serving of a request; the context stack; the making of the target; the threefold testing pipeline), each with its gap named — the pattern of the gaps is itself a finding: every machine in the piece bottoms out in a judgment no state of the machine checks — and one inferred, the life of a cache, drawn in the synthesis scroll, whose illegal combination (COMPILED taken while still GROWING) the piece walks up to in words and cannot rule out in states. The Singular audit opened at 72 residual words and closed at 0: the five authors and the paper's own coinages (the equirational family, neuralware) to the lists, the possessives of the filing's vocabulary beside their precedents, and the plain prose rewritten — lawfully, preparatory, statable, and their kin traded for the tracker's plainer words. Canonical sha 14f88d87...; the registry re-proved in Lean on aletheia-core over the spliced 1,243-entry registry. The Oracle holds at about 75% (68-82), no gate moving: the TRUE gate was already met and a second receipt of a kind already exercised does not move it; the FALSE gate, half-met at the last filing, is untouched — the piece offered nothing the house could refute, and nothing it tried to.

WHAT THE PROCESS TAUGHT. Three things. First, price a paper's claims by their checkable surface, not by their size: this piece's headline numbers are enormous — 291 times cheaper — and every one of them that arithmetic could reach was exact to the rounding, while the numbers that matter most (the accuracies) are exactly the ones no arithmetic can reach. The filing's honesty lives in keeping those apart at the level of the individual concept, not in a caveat at the chapter's end; 1.2.480's scope sentence is the whole lesson in one line. Second, the nearness discipline of the author check cuts both ways: the check exists to catch use without naming, and its equal duty is to say, with the legs shown, when a resemblance is a contrast — a tracker that files only suspicions teaches its reader to suspect everything, and the description-versus-coordinate opposition is worth more filed clean than a vague kinship would be. Third, the synthesis wrote itself from the morning's own work: the unified-backend program rules that a sound distribution carries a declaration and at least one implementation, and a cache entry is that shape already — descriptions as declaration, functions as implementation, compiling as an inflation run once and early. The tracker records the rhyme as a rhyme; the piece knows nothing of the program, and the program's next honest step — a consumer that checks an implementation against its declaration — is the same judge-shaped hole this filing kept meeting in the paper's machines. Two houses, one missing machine.
