on divergence, the defined word coda, two stated state machines, NI 0.0261, the axis judged no in writing, and no restructure pass, the count 536 standing short of the 560 line and Paper 038 of the Paper 042 line. Author check #46 ran on all eight names — the paper read entire and searched, the web, Will's Twitter archive, the construction compared against the dated record — and found no evidence, the descent running cleanly through the ancestors the paper itself cites. The hand count of the registry missed by one entry's classification (the delta scroll files attributed, as every chapter's does), the extractor's count taken as the authority and the drawing written from it; the drawing paragraph itself was grepped for in the built phext before closing, the Paper 037 lesson applied. Re-proof ran on ni-knight as directed, not the hub: the splice verified 1,352 entries inside currentRegistry, fresh project and standing copy both built clean with all exits 0, and Mvo.currentRegistry_accurate depends on [propext] alone. The phextura shadow replayed the transaction exactly (no differing scrolls) and validated green — one false flag along the way traced to my own invocation, a stale conversion report left to default, and corrected by naming it; the Singular audit closed at residual 0, the filing's vocabulary declared in the coined list and the eight names in the names list. Registry after: 1,352 entries — True 533 (436 by stipulation, 97 by verification), Unknown 810, False 2, Fiction 7 — and the Oracle ledger holds at ~75% (68-82), argued in the ledger itself: the False gate is not exercised by a caption's one-unit overstatement, and a met gate does not move for being exercised again.
