Entry 36 — Paper 043 — LOTUS: Bridging the Gap Between Latent and Explicit Reasoning with Looped Transformers, Ying Fan (University of Wisconsin-Madison; Microsoft Research), Anej Svete (ETH Zürich) and Kangwook Lee (University of Wisconsin-Madison; KRAFTON; Ludo Robotics): a network taking-in, leg 5 of the reference walk Will directed on 2026-11-24 — the paper stood at rank 8 of the frontier queue the corpus's own bibliographies make, cited by Chapter 56's paper among the latent-reasoning methods, and the queue record was confirmed from queue.jsonl itself before anything was fetched; outside the pre-registered sample, which closed at Paper 036, so no seal stands and no score is computed. One fetch bought the paper entire (the arXiv HTML of 2606.31779v1, appendices included), and two web searches served the author check's web legs; everything else was local. A v2 stands on arXiv (13 July 2026); the filing reads v1, as the house's passes do, and the caveat at 61.1.4 owns the choice. The work names its phenomenon before its method: latent chain-of-thought matches explicit CoT on small backbones and falls behind beyond a billion parameters, the shortfall widening as the backbone grows — CODI + SIM-CoT level at GPT-2 and 9.2 points behind at 3B — and LOTUS closes that gap by grounding the latents directly. A looped padded Transformer holds K blocks of c latent tokens between question and answer, block i pinned by position to gold CoT step i, refined for R iterations under an input-injected recurrence that re-adds the latent embeddings at every pass and attends throughout to the question's prefix cache, computed once. The grounding is a step loss: every post-loop latent position scored by cross-entropy, through the base model's own LM head, against its step's gold token — direct, parallel, post-loop — beside the answer loss, the two dividing as coverage and selection in the paper's own analysis: the step loss optimizes a parallel chain likelihood whose dropped autoregressive dependence is carried, the paper claims, by the shared latent computation, and the answer loss selects jointly computed states that support the answer. At Llama-3.2-3B the method stands 1.5 points behind explicit CoT in-domain and above it on the out-of-domain average, at two-and-a-half times lower thought latency; an auxiliary-decoder routing matches it at 3B and degrades at small scales; and the analysis reads the trajectory back — the post-loop latents, projected through the head, recover the gold chain at 70.9% top-1, and place graded mass on valid chains never trained on. Integration extended cluster AT for the fourth time, and the extension changes the cluster's posture again: the founding papers read the recurrent trajectory at inference, Paper 040 manufactured it on a frozen checkpoint, Paper 042 audited and priced it — this paper trains it, the first training-time member of the cluster, its trajectory a block grid whose positions carry fixed external referents and whose legibility is a measured property rather than an assumption. Twelve concepts 1.2.588-1.2.599, no held concept revised (the looped Transformer and the recurrent trajectory used exactly as held; latent-explicit complementarity, Paper 042's channels combined, contrasted rather than revised, this paper's latent channel replacing the explicit one at parity), no foundation and no defined word — the imports, the key-value cache and attention above all, already stand — two stated state machines (the looped latent computation; the staged latent curriculum inherited from Coconut's recipe and counted because the filing takes the machine from the work) bringing the held count to 204 (175 stated, 29 inferred), NI 0.0200, the axis judged no in writing. One pressure was recorded and held apart at 61.2.2: the prefix cache, computed once and attended by every iteration, is cluster J's species again — the same look-back Paper 042 recorded against PLT's frozen cache — held apart on the same distinction, c