ses, the web showing the latent-thinking line at Ohio State and the survey literature already citing the work, no tie anywhere. All three authors are new to the book, each carrying the filing's increments whole, True +1 and Unknown +15, and the researchers count rises to 210. Registry after: 1,485 entries — True 554 (444 by stipulation, 110 by verification), Unknown 922 (819 attributed, 60 synthesis, 41 open, 2 by estimate), False 2, Fiction 7 — 610 canonical concepts, and the Oracle ledger holds at ~75% (68-82): TRUE exercised and met, UNKNOWN exercised and met, FALSE not exercised, FICTION untouched. The drawing paragraph and the chapter heading were each grepped in the built phext, exactly once each. Three facts of this pass belong to its own history. First, the registry-proof step ran on the house's own instrument for the second consecutive pass: the TLUF solver's check on the new registry and preserve across the Paper 043 to Paper 044 pair both printed ACCURATE with assumptions: none, the preservation reading 21 additions, no transitions, 1,464 unchanged — the step is routine now, which is what the beachfront sentence looks like when it is working. Second, the pass caught its own form error before the proof legs ran: the chapter scrolls as first written opened in a summary's shape rather than the house's headed form — the delta without its cluster weighing, the work without its state machines stated — and the build was restored from its pre-pass backup and the whole chain re-run with the chapter written in the form the recent passes keep; the registry came out identical, which is how the error is known to have been one of form and not of substance, and the re-run cost one build cycle. Third, the filing's centre of mass was argued, not defaulted: this is the first AT member whose scorer's operational shape belongs to another cluster, and the holding-apart at 62.2.2 is written to be falsifiable — a future member whose scorer reads anything beyond the trajectory itself crosses the line this one walks, and the book will have to choose again. Q210-Q213 open: whether the probe prices the thinking or the problem, difficulty being the confound the pooled training invites; where selection pressure turns into reward hacking of the guiding metric, the paper's own bound loosening as the tilt sharpens; whether LOTUS's alignment training and this selection compose, or spend the same trajectory diversity; and whether correctness is the only axis a latent trajectory can be priced on, the paper's limitations naming the safety and helpfulness dimensions it does not read.
