Entry 43 — Paper 050 — Looped Transformers for Length Generalization: Ying Fan, Yilun Du, Kannan Ramchandran & Kangwook Lee (the University of Wisconsin-Madison; the Massachusetts Institute of Technology; UC Berkeley), 'Looped Transformers for Length Generalization': a network taking-in, leg 12 of the reference walk Will directed on 2026-11-24 — the paper stood at rank 15 of the frontier queue, cited in Chapter 56's bibliography, and the queue record was confirmed from queue.jsonl itself before anything was fetched; the record carried the title and the full byline but no identifier, and the work was identified by them in one search (arXiv:2409.15647); one fetch read the arXiv listing, one fetch bought the paper entire (the arXiv HTML of 2409.15647v1, Sections 1-6, Appendices A-E and the reference list), and two web searches served the author check's web legs — five network operations in all, everything else local. Versions 2-5 stand on the listing, v5 of 12 May 2025, and the ICLR 2025 proceedings version stands with them (proceedings p. 3714); the filing reads v1, as the house's passes do, and the note at 68.1.4 owns the difference. The held text's byline agrees with the queue record exactly — all four names, in order; no correction to the frontier's record was needed beyond filling in the identifier the record lacked. The work asks which algorithmic tasks a looped Transformer can be taught so that it solves them at lengths it never trained on, and answers in three parts. A problem class: n-RASP-L, the tasks whose solution is one RASP-L operation iterated a length-dependent number of times — parity at T(n) = n by shift-and-XOR, copy at T(n) = n by shift, addition at T(n) = n+1 by shifted XOR and AND-carry, the programs printed as listings in its appendix — built on Zhou et al.'s frame, in which a next-token-trained Transformer length-generalizes exactly on the tasks a RASP-L program solves, and iteration is what the rest lack. A training algorithm: supervise only the final answer, after exactly the task's own step count for that example — no intermediate supervision, no chain-of-thought data, the step count the only label beyond the input-output pair — which can teach the steps at all because the mixed lengths of the dataset supervise the same block at every depth, each example's graded final state being a prefix-state of longer runs. And an adaptive inference: the loop runs as many steps as the problem needs, the count supplied by the task's step law or chosen retrospectively by the run's own maximum confidence, the step whose decoded output the model scores lowest in cross-entropy. The results keep the frame's promise: trained on lengths under 20, parity near-perfect past 50 digits and above 0.95 at 100, addition and copy near-perfect ten digits past the training maximum where every next-token baseline fails; pause tokens, which buy horizontal compute, help and do not arrive; and on four of six tasks the loop's output converges after the solving step though nothing trained it to — while on the two where it does not, the confidence rule finds its step anyway. Integration extended cluster AT — the recurrent trajectory — its tenth paper: the trajectory schooled for length, its intermediate steps invented under a supervision that grades only the end. LOTUS (Chapter 61) is this paper's descendant in the same Fan-Lee line and has stood in the book for seven legs; the walk files the ancestor after it, and 68.2.1 weighs what the reversed order shows — the descendant spends gold supervision on every step, the ancestor on none, and the seam between the two filings is the question of who supplies the steps when neither law nor chain is known. AV held apart: no denoising, no learned thought space — the loop runs in the ordinary embedding space. AW held apart: the survey of Chapter 67 describes this family, this very paper standing in its bibliography, but this paper performs an act and does not survey. And the J crossing condition stated at 62.2.2 and weighed at 63.2.2, 64.2.2, 65.2.2, 66.2.2 and 67.2.2 was weighed a seventh time and not crossed — the paper's two stopping rules divide on the condition's two sides: the oracle rule reads the task's step law, a property of the problem known before the run begins, and returns a count, not a verdict; the maximum-confidence rule reads the run's own decoded outputs and keeps the step the run itself scores highest, a signal drawn entirely from the judged object, the same side of the line as Paper 048's convergence exit; no reference beyond the trajectory and the task's own law is consulted, and the crossing is stated falsifiably — a variant whose stopping rule queried a held-out verifier, a second model, or a stored table of correct answers would cross, with Q234 and Q235 keeping the seam open. Twelve concepts 1.2.671-1.2.682, no held concept revised, one foundation laid (RASP-L, 1.3.374 — Zhou et al.'s learnable subset of RASP, the frame's ground term, which did not stand in Section 3), no word coined, two state machines, both stated by the work (the step-supervised loop machine; the adaptive-halting machine), bringing the held count to 218 (187 stated, 31 inferred), NI 0.0176, the axis judged no in writing: the paper claims length generalization for algorithmic tasks, and its one frame-level claim — that perfect length generalization is the signature of having learned the true algorithm — is a claim about generalization, filed as attributed inside 1.2.671. Restructuring Pass #31 fired in-pass — 682 canonical concepts across the 680 line set at Pass #30 — all 682 reviewed, merges none, five candidates weighed and held apart on the record (input injection against LOTUS's input-injected recurrence; the adaptive loop count against inference-time budget adaptation; maximum-confidence stopping against the convergence exit; sequential compute against the survey's horizontal-vertical axis; n-RASP-L against the looped Transformer itself); the next pass falls due at Paper 057 or 700 concepts, whichever arrives first. The house check recomputed the paper's printed arithmetic by script — forty-seven checks, forty-four exact, three tensions, no failures: the three step laws; all six worked examples recomputed from the tasks' definitions; the training ranges and baselines; Table 2 whole (depths 1, 2, 3, 4, 3, 3; intervals 1000, 1000, 1600, 500, 1000, 1000); Table 1 whole, its ascending order matching the text's claim that the looped inference is the slower; Appendix D's complexity statements; the reference sequence [1] to [37]; the four listings; the figure test lengths; the training and evaluation arithmetic. The three tensions, all caveats at 68.1.4 with no False: the Multiplication worked example prints 010010, six digits, where the paper's stated convention — reversed order, length the sum of the lengths — gives five (3x6 = 18 = 0b10010, reversed 01001); the value is right and the string a palindrome, so only the length disagrees with the paper's own rule. Section 6.1.1 sets Addition's step count to the problem length where Proposition 3.4 and Figure 3 give T(n) = n+1 — a one-step discrepancy between the experiment prose and the paper's own proposition. And Table 1 prints NTP-pause's 0.1315 without the seconds suffix every other entry carries. Author check #58 found no evidence of use without naming, and documented one exposure: the paper read entire and scanned — no phext term of any kind, no 'coordinate' either — its thirty-seven references read with it, the built tracker scanned for all four names, the archive searched entire (29,539 tweets, 47,973 likes), the web searched twice, no tie anywhere. Fan and Lee stand in the book already (Paper 043), each carrying True +1 and Unknown +16 from this filing to stand at True 2, Unknown 32; Du and Ramchandran are new, each at True 1, Unknown 16, and the researchers count rises to 242. The archive's one contact stands as it stood at check #51: two of Will's own tweets addressing @Kangwook_Lee — a wave on 2024-09-27, and phext named to him on 2025-04-25 — exposure documented, uptake none, no reply or reference anywhere in the record. Two collisions the check exists to keep: the book's Dus are Yaxin Du (Paper 042) and Hanwen Du (Paper 044), different people at different institutions — Yilun Du, at MIT, is a third man of the name; and Lee's public CV records Ramchandran as his Berkeley doctoral advisor, the paper's senior pair an advisor and his former student — both recorded at 68.1.6. Registry after: 1,614 entries — True 569 (447 by stipulation, 122 by verification), Unknown 1,036 (933 attributed, 60 synthesis, 41 open, 2 by estimate), False 2, Fiction 7 — 682 canonical concepts, and the Oracle ledger holds at ~75% (68-82): TRUE exercised and met, UNKNOWN exercised and met, FALSE not exercised, FICTION untouched. The registry-proof step closed clean: the TLUF solver printing ACCURATE on check and ACCURATE on preserve, 22 additions, no transitions, 1,592 unchanged, assumptions: none. The phextura shadow absorbed the filing natively (base sync clean; 22 inserts, 14 replaces, no removes; every comparable scroll identical to the direct conversion; NI from the transaction log equal to the canonical 12/682; validate.py GREEN entire, run against this pass's own conversion report) and stands advanced. The drawing paragraph and the chapter heading were each grepped in the built phext, exactly once each. Two facts of this pass belong to its own history. First, the walk's order has now twice filed the ground after the building: Huginn, the substrate, arrived ninth among AT's papers, and this paper, the Fan-Lee line's ancestor, arrives after its descendant — the citation graph's order is not the field's chronology, and the book, which files by reference, keeps discovering its foundations late; 68.2.1 is the record of this instance. Second, two defects of the pass itself, owned: the house-check script's first runs failed ten of its checks in three successive drafts, every failure an expectation misstated in the script's own writing — phrases asserted from a skim ('20x deeper', 'batch size of 64') where the paper's words are 'a depth 20 times the depth of the looped block' and 'batch size 64' inside a longer sentence, a reference count taken from a pattern that also caught a body citation, a table read as name-value pairs where the text layer prints two positional blocks — the held text was re-read for each, the expectations corrected, the final run clean at forty-four exact with the three real tensions standing, and nothing was filed from the wrong strings; the pattern is Papers 048's and 049's, and the run record keeps the failures. And the pass's first chapter drafts were written to an older chapter semantics — questions at 2.1, the novelty at 1.5 in the old place — and were rewritten against the current house form (machines at 1.2, questions and novelty-by-author at 1.5, references and imports at 3.1) before integration, when the built Chapter 67 was read as the template; the drafts were never integrated, and the correction cost nothing but the writing. Q234-Q237 open: what the confidence is reading where the loop does not converge; whether the step law itself can be learned, and what would supervise it; whether the method discovers iterations or only fits them; and how much of the length generalization is the loop's and how much the input anchor's.
