Entry 44 — Paper 051 — Defining the mathematical family tree with a minimal programming language: Max Tegmark (the Massachusetts Institute of Technology), the companion paper to his Math Tree Explorer: a Will-posted taking-in, outside the pre-registered sample and outside the network queue — Will posted the bare atlas link in the MOAT chat on 2026-11-24, and the pass was sequenced to file immediately after Paper 050 closed, the reference walk pausing for it and resuming as leg 13. Fifteen network operations in all, single-threaded and at human pace under the netizen rule: the paper itself (mathtree.pdf, 984,766 bytes, sha256 a8e0885a…, last updated 2026-11-23), read entire — Sections 1-4, Appendix A, the reference list; the three reference implementations (mlisp.py, mlisp7.py, mlisp.c); the atlas index page and its six data files (data.js, models_src.js, atlas_src.js, families_src.js, families_auto.js, genealogy_src.js); two GitHub API calls that were abandoned as a counting route when the recursive-tree response truncated; and two web searches for the author check. The work's Lean code was not read: Lean is exiled by Will's ruling of 2026-11-24, and the paper's Lean claims are filed attributed, exactly as Chapter 50 filed its artifact's. What governed the filing was Will's ruling for this taking-in, given minutes after the link: 'we do not wish to observe presentations — we do not care about human legibility — crumble math to first strings.' The chapter therefore files the MLISP string corpus — the definitions as strings over a nine-symbol alphabet, their lengths, their bootstrap order, what they compute when run — and the legible tree the work draws stands in the filing as one concept (1.2.696), the derived view, beneath the thirteen concepts of the corpus itself. The paper defines a Turing-complete language of nine single characters — a b c d f 0 i j k — in which a value is the raw string that builds it ('data is code': 0000ccc is at once the tree, its name, and the program that constructs it, read as the natural 3 by a convention laid on the string from outside), grows its corpus by prefix definitions whose arity is read off their bodies, and climbs from a seventeen-string arithmetic ladder — bodies of 3 to 21 characters, the prime test a four-character string (iibP) standing on the whole ladder beneath it — through integer and rational presentations whose sets and functions are alike strings, to finite structures held as lookup tables and countably infinite ones as halting programs, the triple-dot tableau refused by name as relying on unspecified human intuition. Over the corpus stand two identifications — the structure as an equivalence class of presentations under relabeling (Carnap's definition of 1936, recovered deliberately), and the coarser clone, closure under composition, one rung of an observer's ladder of four equivalences — and a census: structures and clones counted by canonical form, sameness decided by saturation, several clone columns computed for the first time, one cell (the four-element magma clones) left open above 10^5 CPU-years. Integration founded cluster AX — first strings: mathematics as strings that run — its first paper, weighed against four neighbours and held apart from each at the string level: AK nearest, whose formats carry content without interpreting it, where these strings are not carried but run and the content exists only in the running — the format is the machine; AS, whose anatomy decomposes a practice into parts meant to be read, where this corpus climbs a ladder meant to be executed and its taxonomy is the derived view the ruling set aside; AW, whose survey describes a territory it does not contain, where this corpus's records contain the territory itself; AO brushed only, by the Lean claims, and the exile governing the brush. Fourteen concepts 1.2.683-1.2.696, no held concept revised, no foundation laid — the work's ground terms are its own constructions, carried as concepts — one word coined (first strings, 1.3.375, from Will's own phrase in the ruling: the level at which a definition stops being a picture of a thing and is the thing's own construction), two state machines, both stated by the work (the MLISP evaluator, whose named gaps are its missing error state and its unguarded recursions; the clone-saturation machine, whose gap is a state space finite but unbounded by anything humane), bringing the held count to 220 (189 stated, 31 inferred), NI 0.0201, the axis judged no in writing: the paper's claims are definability, equivalence and counting, and its frame-level material descends from the author's earlier mathematical-universe work, carried here as motivation. No restructuring pass fell due — 696 canonical concepts stands short of the 700 line set at Pass #31, Paper 057 not reached; the next pass falls due at Paper 057 or 700 concepts. The house check was the pass's centre of gravity, and it executed the corpus: sixty-nine scripted checks, sixty-nine exact. The paper's two worked traces run as printed — the successor string 0ic on 3 leaving 4, and the minus string jibjbfid, the very program the abstract names, on (3, 1) leaving 2. The whole of Table 3's ladder ran through the reference implementation: constants, successor, 3 + 4 = 7, 5 - 2 = 3, 3 * 4 = 12, both powers, 4! = 24 and 0! = 1, equality and the Boolean rungs, less-than both ways, remainders, divisibility, P, and the prime test true at 2, 7 and 13 and false at 8. Figure 3's raw strings were verified by construction — the natural 3, the integer 2 as 000cc0c, -3 as 00000cccc, the rational -2/3 as 0000ccc0000cccc — and the upper storeys executed from the paper's own Section 2.3 tableaus: integer addition and subtraction through the helper strings A, R and S, the congruence-mod-2 relation through E, and Figure 5's isomorphism pair f and g executed both ways on six values, f carrying each unary string to exactly the binary string the tableau's grammar gives. The seven-symbol packing ran in mlisp7.py (3 + 4 = 7, 7 - 2 = 5, the prime test at 7 and 9); the C implementation, compiled by the house, agreed with the Python on five computations; and all seventeen Table 3 bodies agree, character for character, with Table 1 as the implementation carries it. The corpus was counted from the work's own data files: the model atlas enumerates exactly 88 structures, and the theory tree's 75 nodes resolve to exactly 65 theories — under the paper's own classification, stated in full at 69.1.3 (seven foundational concepts in the data; Functions drawn as a foundational concept in the paper's Figure 1; Triple Fields styled a specific structure; Quadruple Fields marked inconsistent), a boxes-only count of the same file giving 66, the difference carried as a caveat rather than smoothed over. What could not be counted stands attributed at 69.1.4: the 34 formal systems and 14 formal languages, for which no held enumeration exists — the site's formal-system family names six systems — and, with them, the claim of a 195-character MLISP interpreter written in MLISP (the string is not printed; Q241 asks after it) and every Lean claim, including the 43% of Mathlib, which stand as the work's claims about its code under the exile, neither endorsed nor examined. No claim of the work failed as stated; there is no False in this filing. Author check #59 found no evidence of use without naming and no evidence of contact: the paper read entire and scanned — no phext term of any kind, the one 'coordinate' the ordinary word in a physics sentence — its forty-one references read with it, the built tracker scanned for the surname (absent; the author is new to the book, his standing drawn fresh at True 1, Unknown 18, and the researchers count rises to 243), the web searched twice with no tie, and Will's Twitter archive searched entire — the surname exactly once, inside a liked tweet by another account listing level-scales ('Kegan 5, Tegmark 4, Kardashev 3, Kübler-Ross 2, DEFCON 1'), the name as a scale's label: not contact, not uptake, not exposure to the work, recorded precisely as the archive's whole contents on this author. Registry after: 1,638 entries — True 572 (448 by stipulation, 124 by verification), Unknown 1,057 (954 attributed, 60 synthesis, 41 open, 2 by estimate), False 2, Fiction 7 — 696 canonical concepts, and the Oracle ledger holds at ~75% (68-82), bookkeeping only: TRUE exercised and met, UNKNOWN exercised and met, FALSE not exercised, FICTION untouched. The registry-proof step closed clean: the TLUF solver printing ACCURATE on check and ACCURATE on preserve, 24 additions, no transitions, 1,614 unchanged, assumptions: none. The phextura shadow absorbed the filing natively (base sync clean; 24 inserts, 14 replaces, no removes; every comparable scroll identical to the direct conversion; 17 keys minted and one bibliography insert; NI from the transaction log equal to the canonical 14/696; validate.py GREEN entire, run against this pass's own conversion report) and stands advanced. The drawing paragraph and the chapter heading were each grepped in the built phext, exactly once each. Three facts of this pass belong to its own history, owned. First, the check script's first full run failed three of its sixty-nine checks, every failure its own misstated expectation in the pattern of Papers 048-050: a binary zero built by the general spine rule where the tableau gives the atom itself for n = 0; a prime assertion at input 1, below the domain Table 3 itself states, where the string applies b to the atom and returns no value — the boundary now recorded at 69.1.4 as a confirmation of the stated domain rather than a defect; and a reference count taken by a pattern that also caught a wrapped citation inside entry [25]'s own text. Each was corrected against the held text and the run record keeps the failures. Second, the drawing paragraph's first build carried a mispredicted split — 952 attributed and 62 by synthesis, where the extractor's defaults give both of the chapter's Section 2 scrolls to attributed, 954 and 60 — caught at Phase A, corrected in the text, and rebuilt before the final build, so the paragraph in the phext carries the measured numbers; the totals (572, 1,057, 1,638) were right from the first build. Third, the pass's first integration script was written from a remembered pattern rather than from integrate_p050.py itself and failed on its anchors; it was discarded and rewritten line for line against the real script — the standing lesson of Paper 047, relearned at the cost of one failed run and nothing else. Q238-Q241 open: whether a structure or a clone has a canonical simplest presentation; the lowest group order between 24 and 260 at which two distinct groups are compositionally equivalent; whether the four-element magma row of the clone census can be brought within reach; and where the claimed 195-character self-interpreter stands, and whether it runs.
