Entry 45 — Paper 052 — AIME 2025: OpenCompass (the Shanghai AI Laboratory's evaluation platform), a benchmark artifact rather than a paper — leg thirteen of the network walk, queue rank 16 of the reference frontier, the key cited by Chapter 56's paper (LoopCD) in its evaluation apparatus and reported against again in Chapters 57 and 65. The queue record carried the title and the organization but no identifier; identified by title and organization in one search, to the dataset's home on Hugging Face. Seven network operations in all, single-threaded and at human pace under the netizen rule: the identification search, one Hugging Face API fetch, the three held files, and two web searches for the author check. The held material is small and entire: the dataset card (README.md, 448 bytes, sha256 43ac9ef2…), aime2025-I.jsonl (5,764 bytes, sha256 b91b3c96…) and aime2025-II.jsonl (6,285 bytes, sha256 16a2dcfb…), held at repo HEAD a6ad95f611d72cf628a80b58bd0432ef6638f958, last modified 2025-02-25, 12,318 downloads at the held state — the American Invitational Mathematics Examination of February 2025 transcribed as data, thirty problems in two sittings of fifteen, each row a question string and an answer string and nothing else, under the MIT licence. Integration founded cluster AY — THE ANSWER KEY: THE MEASURE AS A FIXED TABLE — its first paper, weighed against five neighbours and held apart from each at the artifact's own level: AT first, because the citing Chapter 56 founds it — AT's papers perform acts on trajectories and report the outcomes against this key, and to file the yardstick among the measured would confuse the instrument with its object; O, whose statistics price judges from logged records — the key is the held-out material such pricing consumes, not a criterion; AV, AW and AX in turn — nothing generated, nothing described (the artifact contains no prose at all), and strings that are compared rather than run, the pointed inversion of Chapter 69's corpus; AK brushed, the rows riding in a format no format claim is made of. Cluster J was weighed from the reference's side for the first time: the answer key is literally the third device the crossing condition's falsifiable form names — a stored table of correct answers, consulted for verdicts whose evidence lies beyond every judged object — and the verdict is NOT CROSSED, on the distinction that the condition governs mechanisms and this work contains none: it judges nothing, consults nothing, and is consulted by everything; the seam does not move, but it has a resident on its far side now, and Q242 asks who files the crossing when a mechanism consults the key mid-computation. Twelve concepts 1.2.697-1.2.708 file the instrument's anatomy — the benchmark artifact itself (the species the book used for fifty-one papers and never filed), the integer answer contract, the answer key, the exact-match verdict, the two sittings, the transcribed examination, the measure's half-life, the measure as training data, the thirty-problem grain, the bare row, the sitting order, and the key's borrowed authority — no held concept revised (the book used measures throughout and filed none; the filing adds the instrument and changes no held claim; pass@k at 1.3.365 is used, not revised), no foundation laid, no word coined, the axis judged no in writing: the artifact claims no dimension of the models it measures, and its commensurability across models is the examination's design, filed as concepts. Two state machines, both inferred (the scoring machine — extract, compare, count — whose named gaps are the unextractable right answer and the malformed key row; the circulation machine — fresh, circulating, absorbed — whose gap is that absorption is invisible from the artifact), bringing the held count to 222 (189 stated, 33 inferred), NI 0.0169. Restructuring Pass #32 fell due in this taking-in — 708 canonical concepts crossing the 700 line set at Pass #31 — and closed with five merges weighed and held apart (the half-life from absorption, decay being passive and absorption an act; the answer key from J's oracle reference, the distance between them being the seam itself; the exact-match verdict from pass@k, a rule from its aggregate; the grain from the easy judge, the material from the procedure; the two sittings from the bare row, partition from form), no splits, none retired; the next pass falls due at Paper 057 or 720 canonical concepts. The house check re-derived the key from the problems: twenty-nine scripted checks, twenty-nine exact. The artifact's structure entire — fifteen rows a sitting, row keys exactly question and answer, thirty distinct questions, twenty-nine answers bare integers in [0, 999], the repo inventory, the card's two configs and MIT licence — and one cross-check against the book itself: Chapter 57's case study names 821 against a base decoder's 271, and sitting I's pairing problem carries 821 in the key. Then twenty-two of the thirty answers recomputed from their problem statements: sitting I's first eleven and its fifteenth — the base sum 70; the heptagon's 588, its given quadrilateral area forcing sin θ = 6/13; the flavors' 16; the lattice pairs 117 counted whole; the permutations' 279; the trapezoid's 504; the pairing probability's 821 over all 10,395 pairings; the tangent condition's 77; the rotated parabola's 62; the Sudoku band's 81; the sawtooth's 259, its thirty-five intersection ordinates summed exactly to (1 + 5√185)/68; the cube triples' 735 by residue convolution — and sitting II's first five and its seventh through eleventh: the collinear area 468, the divisor sum 49, the grid colorings 82, the telescoping product 106, the nine-point arcs 336, the divisor-lcm subsets 237, the greedy coins 610 of a thousand, the trigonometric zeros 149 (the sine's zero level contributing nine roots in the interval, not ten, its endpoints excluded), the chair subsets 907, the 24-gon's matchings 113 with the diameter step contributing exactly one. The eight answers not re-derived stand attributed at 70.1.4 on the examination's authority, beside the pass's one format defect: II-5's stored answer is the string '336^\circ', the only one of thirty not a bare integer — its numeric content verified, its form defective, a raw-string scorer failing every correct response on that row; Q243 asks what normalization the consuming harnesses applied. Author check #60 found no evidence of use without naming and no evidence of contact: the held material scanned entire (no term of Will's; 'coordinate' four times, each the ordinary word inside a problem), the built tracker scanned for the name — zero occurrences before this chapter, the artifact having entered the queue from Chapter 56's bibliography without its publisher reaching the chapter scrolls — Will's Twitter archive searched entire (zero occurrences), and the web searched twice with no tie, its one Bickford being Freddie Bickford Smith, an Oxford researcher, another man, kept apart; OpenCompass is entered fresh at 1.5.6 as a company, the fourth in the book, its vector True +1, Unknown +16, the named researchers standing at 243. Registry after: 1,659 entries — True 574 (448 by stipulation, 126 by verification), Unknown 1,076 (972 attributed, 60 by synthesis, 42 open, 2 by estimate), False 2, Fiction 7 — 708 canonical concepts, and the Oracle ledger holds at ~75% (68-82), bookkeeping only: TRUE exercised and met, UNKNOWN exercised and met, FALSE not exercised, FICTION untouched. The registry-proof step closed clean: the TLUF solver printing ACCURATE on check and ACCURATE on preserve, 21 additions, no transitions, 1,638 unchanged, assumptions: none. The phextura shadow absorbed the filing natively (base sync clean; 21 inserts, 14 replaces, no removes; every comparable scroll identical to the direct conversion; 14 keys minted and one bibliography insert; NI from the transaction log equal to the canonical 12/708; validate.py GREEN entire, run against this pass's own conversion report) and stands advanced. The drawing paragraph and the chapter heading were each grepped in the built phext, exactly once each. Three facts of this pass belong to its own history, owned. First, the check script's first run failed four of its twenty-nine checks, every failure its own misstated expectation in the pattern of Papers 048-051: a probability taken over 2^15 − 1 subsets where the sample space is all 2^15; the negative-sine branch of the trigonometric count missing its period offset, six roots short; the diameter step of the matching count taken as 2^12 matchings where the step graph is itself the single matching; and the sawtooth sum's constant term dropped in extraction, one short of 259 — each corrected against the problem statements and the run re-made clean before filing, the failures standing in the record at 70.1.3; and the clean re-run overwrote the first run's record file, so the four failures survive as enumerated in the chapter and here, not as a kept log — a slip against the house's own run-record practice, recorded rather than smoothed over. Second, the drawing paragraph's first build carried a mispredicted split — True 575 with 449 by stipulation and Unknown 1,075 with 41 open, where the extractor's defaults give the chapter's references scroll to attributed and its questions scroll to open: True 574 (448 by stipulation), Unknown 1,076 (42 open) — caught at Phase A, corrected in the text, and rebuilt before the final build, so the paragraph in the phext carries the measured numbers; the entry total (1,659) was right from the first build. Third, the pass's first integration script carried one wrong assertion of its own — the restructure-log anchor checked at sixty-four characters where the house takes sixty — caught before any edit ran and corrected; the integration then ran clean, all nineteen edits and both inserts at their anchors. Q242-Q245 open: who files the crossing when a mechanism consults the key mid-computation; what normalization the harnesses applied to the malformed row, and whether every AIME 2025 figure in the book carries its silent one-row handicap; whether a detectable date exists after which scores on this set measure memory rather than reasoning; and what completing the audit of the eight unrecomputed entries would take.
